<h2 id="quick-answer">How do you support your pregnant wife?</h2>
<p><strong>Listen to what feels hardest, take ownership of everyday work, and prepare for the baby alongside her. Handle meals, household tasks, and shared logistics without waiting for instructions. Ask what support she wants, respect her decisions, and follow through consistently.</strong></p>
<p>You can be thrilled about becoming a dad and still be missing what is happening in your own kitchen. She is exhausted. Dinner is undecided. There are three appointment reminders on her phone. You ask, “What can I do?” and somehow that becomes one more thing she has to figure out.</p>
<p>The question comes from a good place. But if you want to support your pregnant wife, the useful shift is from being available to being responsible for something. She should be able to stop thinking about dinner because she knows you have it handled.</p>
<p>At Dudela, “Be The Partner She Needs” is one of our six pillars for a reason. Fatherhood starts in how you show up for the person in front of you, well before you hold the baby.</p>
